    <h3 id=3D"DataAnalysis:R2PMSubadvisor-R2PMsub-advisorsinPROD(RAW)">R2 P=
M sub-advisors in PROD (RAW)</h3>
    <p>Definition: An active R2 user id who is assigned to one or many PM s=
ub-advisor RR codes</p>
    <p>Source file folder in SharePoint:&nbsp;<a class=3D"external-link" hr=
ef=3D"https://cbncnbccs.sharepoint.com/:f:/r/sites/Compass-X/Shared%20Docum=
ents/Product%20Management/Multi-Firm%20Users?csf=3D1&amp;web=3D1&amp;e=3DNV=
kZBg" rel=3D"nofollow">NBIN Product Team &gt; Product Management &gt; Multi=
-Firm Users</a></p>
    <p>Collection method: The source file is collected on Mar 16, 2026, b<s=
pan style=3D"letter-spacing: 0.0px;">y querying the NBCN_OneClick database =
in prod SQL server directly</span></p>
    <ul>
     <li>IMPORTANT: The raw data file contains duplicated PM sub-advisor RR=
 codes for 6 users; in other words, ~0.8% of users<span style=3D"letter-spa=
cing: 0.0px;"> have at least one RR code </span>repeated within their own R=
R list<span style=3D"letter-spacing: 0.0px;">. Besides, the eligibility of =
the RR codes (inactive? non-existent?) are not screened yet. The <strong>da=
ta error</strong> will be addressed in the "normalized" analysis section be=
low.</span></li>
    </ul>
    <p><br></p>
    <p><span style=3D"font-weight: 600;letter-spacing: -0.003em;">In a glan=
ce</span></p>
