 <div class=3D"columnLayout single" data-layout=3D"single">
  <div class=3D"cell normal" data-type=3D"normal">
   <div class=3D"innerCell">
    <p><br></p>
    <h3 id=3D"DataAnalysis:R2PMSubadvisor-R2PMsub-advisorsinPROD(Deduplicat=
ed+Normalized)"><span style=3D"font-size: 16.0px;font-weight: bold;letter-s=
pacing: -0.006em;">R2 PM sub-advisors in PROD (Deduplicated + Normalized)</=
span></h3>
    <p>Definition: A<span style=3D"letter-spacing: 0.0px;">&nbsp;</span>ful=
ly normalized file<span style=3D"letter-spacing: 0.0px;">&nbsp;with </span>=
one PM sub=E2=80=91advisor RR code per user per row<span style=3D"letter-sp=
acing: 0.0px;">, </span>deduplicated per user<span style=3D"letter-spacing:=
 0.0px;">, and added the </span>FirmId<span style=3D"letter-spacing: 0.0px;=
"> of the PM sub-advisor RR code</span></p>
    <p>Source file folder in SharePoint:&nbsp;<a class=3D"external-link" hr=
ef=3D"https://cbncnbccs.sharepoint.com/:f:/r/sites/Compass-X/Shared%20Docum=
ents/Product%20Management/Multi-Firm%20Users?csf=3D1&amp;web=3D1&amp;e=3DNV=
kZBg" rel=3D"nofollow">NBIN Product Team &gt; Product Management &gt; Multi=
-Firm Users</a></p>
    <p>Collection method: Normalize the raw file, left join <strong>CATRRM =
(AS400 data)</strong>, and append the required data columns to show the fir=
m of the RR code and RR code status</p>
    <p><br></p>
   </div>
  </div>
 </div>
 <div class=3D"columnLayout single" data-layout=3D"single">
  <div class=3D"cell normal" data-type=3D"normal">
   <div class=3D"innerCell">
    <p>The followings issues worth to be further studied and mitigated.</p>
    <h4 id=3D"DataAnalysis:R2PMSubadvisor-1.ClientCodeismissing">1. Client =
Code is missing&nbsp;</h4>
    <ul>
     <li data-uuid=3D"7eda1f9d-3934-4391-8fbe-152586430d06">The&nbsp;<stron=
g>ClientCode </strong>is missing for the following 9 R2 user profiles becau=
se&nbsp;</li>
    </ul>
    <p style=3D"margin-left: 40.0px;">(a) Their repcodes is blank, or</p>
    <p style=3D"margin-left: 40.0px;">(b) The Branch Code (field: RRM_INT_B=
RN_CODE) of their repcodes is blank in CATRRM (AS400 data)</p>
    <ul>
     <li data-uuid=3D"4d291f9a-0b3f-46cb-a2c2-dcf413acc13a">Why don't they =
have repcodes?&nbsp;=20
      <ul>
       <li data-uuid=3D"9041345c-11f5-43aa-914f-c0689f0688e5">Are they not =
our client, e.g. Their R2 user profile is set up under a client firm but th=
ey do not work for that firm?</li>
       <li data-uuid=3D"f47ba71e-93aa-4e1d-9161-6ac62741b21a">Do they not h=
ave access to client accounts in their primary firm?&nbsp;</li>
       <li data-uuid=3D"c1bf92f0-dbc5-4dc6-8234-98c35e78e80a">Maybe they ha=
ve a separate user profile in their primary firm and this user profile is f=
or PM sub-advising client accounts only? Do they not know how to set up PM =
sub-advisor RR codes IN their primary user profile? &nbsp;&nbsp;</li>
      </ul></li>
     <li>Why aren't certain RR codes (e.g. Q1P* in the shared broker code, =
QCPM) assigned a Client Code in CATRRM table (field name: RRM_INT_BRN_CODE)=
?=20
      <ul>
       <li data-uuid=3D"455066f3-6083-43f2-9435-5ae1b03b72ae">Is it data er=
ror?&nbsp;</li>
       <li data-uuid=3D"c03217f4-cee1-407f-99f5-e177dfc76115">Are the RR co=
des still legit?&nbsp;</li>
      </ul></li>
     <li data-uuid=3D"5f930b39-dd87-4ade-8e33-d898f0b75aa7"><u><strong>Scop=
e impacts:&nbsp;</strong></u>
      <ul>
       <li data-uuid=3D"305565c9-97a1-4388-9e8e-4a536a5236c1">Is it a valid=
 use case that some PM sub-advisors are not employed by any of our client f=
irms, hence, do not have a "home firm"?</li>
       <li data-uuid=3D"54453bf4-06d6-43b1-b542-6b0ff1ba342e">Would the mis=
sing Client Code for the shared brokers (e.g. QCPM) in CATRRM table breakin=
g the firm identifier reference in Firm360?</li>
      </ul></li>
    </ul>
    <p><br></p>
    <div class=3D"table-wrap">
     <table class=3D"wrapped confluenceTable">
      <tbody>
       <tr>
        <th scope=3D"col" class=3D"confluenceTh">BrokerCode</th>
        <th scope=3D"col" class=3D"confluenceTh"><span style=3D"color:#c937=
2c;">ClientCode</span></th>
        <th scope=3D"col" class=3D"confluenceTh">userid</th>
        <th scope=3D"col" class=3D"confluenceTh">firstname</th>
        <th scope=3D"col" class=3D"confluenceTh">lastname</th>
        <th scope=3D"col" class=3D"confluenceTh">EmailAddr</th>
        <th scope=3D"col" class=3D"confluenceTh"><span style=3D"color:#c937=
2c;">repcodes</span></th>
        <th scope=3D"col" class=3D"confluenceTh">PM_subadvisor_rr_codes</th=
>
       </tr>
       <tr>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">ICPMB</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Allan.Meyer1</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Allan</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Meyer</td>
        <td colspan=3D"2" class=3D"confluenceTd"><a class=3D"external-link"=
 href=3D"mailto:allan.meyer@wellington-altus.ca" rel=3D"nofollow">allan.mey=
er@wellington-altus.ca</a></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">A6LA,A6LB,A6LN,A6LO,A6LE</td>
       </tr>
       <tr>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">ICPMB</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">David.OKeeffe1</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">David</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">O'Keeffe</td>
        <td colspan=3D"2" class=3D"confluenceTd"><a class=3D"external-link"=
 href=3D"mailto:dokeeffe@bcvfinancial.com" rel=3D"nofollow">dokeeffe@bcvfin=
ancial.com</a></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">R3Z4</td>
       </tr>
