    <p style=3D"margin-left: 40.0px;"><br></p>
    <h4 id=3D"DataAnalysis:R2PMSubadvisor-3.User'sPMsub-advisorRRcodeiswith=
intherangeoftheirprimaryfirm"><span>3. User's PM sub-advisor RR code is wit=
hin the range of their primary firm</span></h4>
    <ul>
     <li data-uuid=3D"18ce5aff-e3d5-4217-ba43-4ca22c27eae6">Definition: A u=
ser's PM sub-advisor RR code is within the range of their primary firm, whi=
ch means their firm Id is the same as the firm id of their PM sub-advisor R=
R codes=20
      <ul>
       <li>
        <p>(BrokerCode =3D=3D RRM_BKR_CODE) AND <span style=3D"letter-spaci=
ng: 0.0px;">(ClientCode =3D=3D RRM_INT_BRN_CODE)</span></p></li>
      </ul></li>
     <li data-uuid=3D"45b4ba29-6bc4-4d78-9193-439591797173">Findings:&nbsp;=
=20
      <ol>
       <li data-uuid=3D"9bfd4b78-b2bf-4ac2-8f41-58d167d06376">Some RR codes=
 are repeated in both fields</li>
       <li data-uuid=3D"e577f35c-1fba-4437-8f36-de866117b430">For RR codes =
which are not repeated, they are in their firm range of the user's firm&nbs=
p;</li>
      </ol></li>
     <li data-uuid=3D"ea81d66d-0664-4606-82eb-68d2eabe53e9">Why are some PM=
 sub-advisor RR codes repeated in the user's repcodes?=20
      <ul>
       <li>
        <p>Data input error?&nbsp;</p></li>
       <li data-uuid=3D"0586c939-3ef8-4fb9-9341-aab263b80660">A hack to tri=
gger "PM sub-advisor functionalities"? What is it?</li>
      </ul></li>
     <li data-uuid=3D"9b9c2100-c6c0-410e-b85b-9de92f1749d6">For RR codes wh=
ich are not repeated, why not putting the PM sub-advisor RR codes in their =
repcode field?=20
      <ul>
       <li>
        <p>Are they not supposed to have access to the client accounts in t=
he sub-advising range?</p></li>
       <li data-uuid=3D"cf419c60-8e6b-4c0f-a96c-f7d1089a9805">Is it intenti=
onal that they have different roles on different range of client accounts w=
ithin their firm?</li>
       <li data-uuid=3D"de7d17d3-3da3-410c-9231-6dd54e9e8f99">Is there a le=
git case that a user would sub-advise client accounts within their firm, pr=
obably managed by another IA?</li>
       <li data-uuid=3D"fb8f8858-d5ec-4e9a-bea6-e13d75ef59c4">Is there a me=
rge or acquisition such that the firm range has been expanded but the user =
profile settings have not been updated?</li>
      </ul></li>
     <li><u><strong>Scope impacts:&nbsp;</strong></u>
      <ul>
       <li>
        <p>Is there a confusion of the PM sub-advisor RR code field, causin=
g data input error?</p></li>
       <li data-uuid=3D"ea0e9db5-ec27-4d14-a6f4-f9dc31eaccd0">Is there a de=
sign flaw in any application, forcing clients to add their firm's RR codes =
to the PM sub-advisor RR code field on purpose?</li>
       <li data-uuid=3D"f8007b3c-23f2-431e-a6ca-190e2b9701a0">Is there a la=
ck of user attestation to maintain the data integrity &amp; accuracy?</li>
      </ul></li>
    </ul>
    <p><br></p>
    <p><strong>In a glance</strong></p>
    <div class=3D"table-wrap">
     <table class=3D"relative-table wrapped confluenceTable" style=3D"width=
: 95.4005%;">
